{"title":"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 25","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_25\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 25</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_25\">Problem 25</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 25\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A square with side length 2 and a circle share the same center. The total area of the regions that are inside the circle and outside the square is equal to the total area of the regions that are outside the circle and inside the square. What is the radius of the circle?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c667941886cc09d8e6a51330698d67e111d5d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair a=(4,4), b=(0,0), c=(0,4), d=(4,0), o=(2,2); draw(a--d--b--c--cycle); draw(circle(o, 2.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b556a22bc859e3703d729621b735c0cf5b33e779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{\\pi}} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{1+\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\sqrt{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"457\" height=\"45\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the region within the circle and square be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. In other words, it is the area inside the circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a97e441a34ebf86ea7219135654dee4cc708827.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{and}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"11\" /> the square.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius. We know that the area of the circle minus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to the area of the square, minus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> . \n</p><p>We get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/4/bc418ee0bde9070a82f9fbd3c88a86c641c6056b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2 -a=4-a$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cfce3b95bf0893ae1b312826d50069fd156720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2=\\frac{4}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/8175536d7e2657e855aebae367a9525181957321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{\\pi}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"61\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6bde92204cc05153ce896369c086bbe5fe711a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{\\pi}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"76\" height=\"52\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We realize that since the areas of the regions outside of the circle and the square are equal to each other, the area of the circle must be equal to the area of the square.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/9/509f8bda5c42503bae4ae02949d58bdd4e561ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi r^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33cfce3b95bf0893ae1b312826d50069fd156720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r^2=\\frac{4}{\\pi}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"54\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/7/8175536d7e2657e855aebae367a9525181957321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{\\pi}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"61\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/b/c6bde92204cc05153ce896369c086bbe5fe711a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{\\pi}}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"76\" height=\"52\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=2763\">https://youtu.be/abSgjn4Qs34?t=2763</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xdeWCR666q8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xdeWCR666q8</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_25&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8\" title=\"2005 AMC 8\">2005 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2005\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 24\">Problem 24</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/inde